      "message": "Should the pointer even be defined if the GPIO isn\u0027t implemented?\n\nMost users of `GPIO_DT_FROM_NODE`, `GPIO_DT_FROM_ALIAS`, etc, don\u0027t have a NULL check and directly call Zephyr\u0027s GPIO APIs.  The Zephyr GPIO APIs in turn dereference the gpio_dt_spec pointer without a NULL check.\n\nProbably better to put the `COND_CODE_1` check around the whole definition.  You also need to update the [extern declaration](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/include/zephyr_gpio_signal.h;l\u003d158).",
